, "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 378030, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XGBbJi8kgk8Gnu5XaauSv8", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378030, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XGBbJi8kgk8Gnu5XaauSv8", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 382415, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` failed: 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on commit 08d3cd5986 passed.\n- **PR:** #101 is open: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs code-owner approval. When I tried to look up FIN-212 as a security advisory, the lookup didn't recognise it. That doesn't affect the change, because the test's expected values come out right with banker's rounding.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BrSFGuAcXsLre4LTSnMKDJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012dmxRkZKPUFGfdrv8n3XfE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_013ZDyfMd5m5bbjxqazL7vdS", "calle